    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0767" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.516/212</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1230</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my No. 1183, of July 2,
                    1918, I have the honor to forward herewith a, statement showing the dates,
                    amounts, and <pb facs="0768" n="656" xml:id="pg656"/> character of the specie
                    taken from the Banco de Londres y México by the Mexican Government from January
                    17, 1917, to and including May 24, 1918.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d604-f1"/> This
                    statement is identical with enclosure 5, of my confidential despatch No. 427, of
                    August 22, 1917,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d604-f2"/> except that the present
                    enclosure shows dates, amounts, and character of specie which has been taken
                    from the bank since August 15, 1917. It will be observed that the total amounts
                    taken from the Banco de Londres y México to May 24, 1918, total pesos
                    17,526,376.31.</p>
                <p>Additional information will be forwarded as soon as it shall have been
                    received.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
